From bf5398259bda3084105ddb4e46a9fde1b8da568f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Marschner <alex.marschner@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:36:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Play a staff that %%staffnonote hides, and give it its line's
 time
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

%%staffnonote 0 hides a staff on any line where it has no notes, and the
parser does it by deleting the staff from line.staff. The sequencer and
the timing layer follow a voice through the tune by its position on each
line, so every staff after a hidden one is read as the voice above it,
and a hidden voice loses the time of the lines it is hidden on: tracks
merge, voices start at 0, and the cursor jumps between lines.

The hidden staff stays out of line.staff, so the notation is unchanged,
and is kept in line.hiddenStaffs with its position. The sequencer plays
its rests, so every voice keeps its own track and time — the same notes
as without the directive. The timing layer matches each drawn voice to
its tune voice by that position, and gives a hidden voice its rests,
bars and tempo marks as elements that take time and make no event.

Without any hidden staff, makeVoicesArray and the sequencer run exactly
the code they ran before.

Tests in tests/synth/staffnonote.test.js; 14 of the 29 fail without the
change.
